 "register_statement": "The A bank is 44 criteria written in OLYMPIAD WRITE-UP language (plan before machinery, one line of attack carried to an endpoint, decisive reason extractable in a sentence, symbols defined before use, care spent where the difficulty is), GEPA-revised and Gemma-4-31B judged on the bank's 0.0/0.5/1.0 + NA scale. The corpus is AoPS forum SOLUTIONS shown with their competition problem, and the outcome is whether the solution takes the SAME APPROACH as the editorial/wiki write-up. Three register mismatches are recorded up front: (i) the bank is written about WRITE-UP QUALITY while y is APPROACH IDENTITY against an unseen reference, so a beautifully written solution by a different route is a negative -- this is the cell's whole point; (ii) the judge never sees the editorial, by design, so no criterion can be about resemblance to it; (iii) an applicability gate fires on 22.8% of cells, mostly on short solutions that give a criterion nothing to bite on. No cosine threshold decides identity anywhere in this campaign.",
